---
// src/components/ui/HeroScatterDecoration.astro
// Purely decorative scattered-shape layer for the hero. SUPERSEDES the
// previous white/paper-toned starfield version — that pass is fully
// replaced, not layered alongside this one (per the standing "one
// decorative pattern per component" rule).
//
// Source: converted from an approved static HTML preview
// (`hero-scatter-preview.html`) showing five floating "glass/chrome"
// panels — soft frosted rectangles with a highlight streak and a subtle
// color tint on select shapes — toggleable in the preview between a dark
// and a light hero background. Only the LIGHT-background version is
// built here: Hero.astro's background is moving to the light iridescent
// gradient per the redesign plan, so this component targets that end
// state. (No dark-mode variant exists in this file — if the dark
// background ships instead, this file needs a follow-up pass, not a
// runtime toggle; the preview's toggle bar and "headline sits here"
// label were both preview-only scaffolding and are not present below.)
//
// DESIGN SYSTEM NOTE (per CLAUDE.md Section 4.5 — Per-Page
// Inspiration-Driven Design): the approved preview is the authoritative
// design source for THIS component's shape language (frosted-glass
// panels), which is not one of DESIGN_SYSTEM.md Section 7.5's approved
// decorative patterns — that override is expected and is not flagged as
// a deviation, per 4.5's explicit instruction. What still stays fixed
// per 4.5's own carve-out: the three signal colors below are exactly
// DESIGN_SYSTEM.md's approved blue-600/teal-600/amber-500 tokens (no new
// tint hues introduced), and every zero-tolerance process rule in
// CLAUDE.md Sections 1/2/5 (layout ownership, no inline style, full-file
// delivery, etc.) still applies in full.
//
// Colors/materials: shape fill is a `bg-white` gradient (white is
// already a sanctioned base tone in DESIGN_SYSTEM.md Section 4's
// bg-paper/bg-white section-background rhythm) at varying opacity to
// read as frosted glass; select shapes carry a color-tint overlay using
// only the three approved signal tokens (blue-600, teal-600, amber-500).
// Nothing here is an inline style="..." attribute — all variation is
// Tailwind utility classes, standard-scale values, or (for keyframe
// animation only, same as the previous starfield file) a <style> block.
//
// TEXT-COLUMN CLEARANCE: Hero.astro centers its content in a `max-w-2xl`
// column with no max-width on the `<section>` itself. Like the previous
// version, this component only renders at `lg:` and up (applied by the
// consumer via `class="hidden lg:block"` on Hero.astro's usage of this
// component, not hardcoded here) — so the narrowest viewport is 1024px,
// where the centered column spans ~17%–83%. Every shape below sits
// within roughly -6% to 6% of the left/right edges (per the approved
// preview's own edge-hugging placements), well clear of that column at
// every `lg:`+ width.
//
// WRAPPER CLEARANCE — CORRECTED, NOT JUST COPIED: the previous starfield
// file's wrapper used `top-40 sm:top-48 lg:top-56`, matching a padding
// scale Hero.astro's <section> used to have. Hero.astro's own history
// (see its "PILL → FULL-WIDTH BAR" pass comment) shows that top padding
// was later tightened to `pt-24 sm:pt-28 lg:pt-32` — the starfield
// file's top offset was never updated to match and is stale. Copying
// those old top-40/48/56 values forward here would reintroduce the
// exact header-clearance bug this wrapper exists to prevent, just with
// wrong numbers pointed at padding that no longer exists. This file uses
// `top-24 sm:top-28 lg:top-32`, matching Hero.astro's <section> padding
// as it actually stands today. Bottom offset (`bottom-28 sm:bottom-40`)
// matches Hero.astro's unchanged `pb-28 sm:pb-40` and needed no
// correction. Same underlying logic as before either way: positioned
// against the section's real padded content box, never `inset-0`.
//
// STACKING ORDER: kept at `-z-[5]`, matching the previous file and
// Hero.astro's own explicit comment that this layer must sit less
// negative than the hero-grain layer's `-z-[9]` (so grain paints first/
// furthest back, this shape layer paints just in front of it, both
// still behind the `z-auto` in-flow content). This is NOT swapped for a
// standard `-z-10` utility: `-z-10` is more negative than `-z-[9]` and
// would flip the intended paint order, putting these shapes behind the
// grain instead of in front of it. Flagged per the "don't quietly
// invent a value" rule, but this bracket value is preserved deliberately
// (it encodes real cross-component stacking order, not a free
// decorative choice) rather than replaced.

export interface Props {
  class?: string;
}

const { class: className } = Astro.props;

// ⚠️ Flags (per CLAUDE.md Section 3 "stop and flag" rule) — visual
// effects from the preview that don't map cleanly onto an existing
// Tailwind utility or a DESIGN_SYSTEM.md token, and how each was
// resolved instead of silently inventing a new value:
//
// 1. Panel box-shadow: the preview uses a custom tinted, multi-layer
//    shadow (large soft drop shadow + two inset highlight/shading
//    layers) with hand-picked rgba stops. Tailwind has no utility for a
//    custom-color drop shadow or a dual inset shadow without arbitrary
//    values. Resolved to the nearest STANDARD shadow scale step,
//    `shadow-2xl`, and the inset highlight/shading layers were dropped
//    rather than approximated with bracket syntax. Visual effect is
//    close but flatter than the preview's glass depth — worth a design
//    check before shipping if that depth matters.
// 2. Panel corner radius: preview uses a fixed 18px. Nearest standard
//    Tailwind step is `rounded-2xl` (16px), which also matches this
//    design system's existing Card radius convention (DESIGN_SYSTEM.md
//    Section 3), so it was used both as the closest match and as the
//    more "in-system" choice over an arbitrary `rounded-[18px]`.
// 3. Panel width/height: preview uses exact pixel dimensions (e.g.
//    220x320, 260x220). None of these are covered by CLAUDE.md's
//    decorative-transform exception (only rotate/translate/position are
//    listed, not size), so each was mapped to the nearest standard
//    Tailwind w-/h- scale step instead (e.g. 220→w-56, 320→h-80 exactly;
//    260→w-64, 220→h-56; 160→w-40/h-40 exact; 300→w-72, 260→h-64;
//    120→w-28, 220→h-56). Shapes read slightly different in exact
//    proportion from the preview but stay recognizably the same
//    composition.
// 4. `skew-x-[...]`/`skew-y-[...]`: CLAUDE.md's decorative-transform
//    exception names `rotate-[...]`, `translate-[...]`, and
//    `top/left/right/bottom-[...]` explicitly, but doesn't name skew.
//    Skew is used here anyway (it's what gives the panels their
//    glass-plane, not-just-a-rotated-rectangle look, and is compositing
//    with rotation the same way translate would) — treated as covered
//    in spirit, but flagged since it isn't literally on the list.
// 5. Highlight streak blur: preview uses `blur(6px)`. Mapped to the
//    nearest standard step, `blur-sm` (4px) — Tailwind has no 6px step.
//
// Confirmed: this is the LIGHT-background variant only (per the task —
// Hero.astro is moving to a light gradient). The preview's dark-stage
// styling was not built here.
//
// Animation: kept, not simplified or dropped. The preview's three
// float keyframes (subtle translate + a touch of added rotation at the
// midpoint, looping) are reproduced as three named animations, same
// mechanism the previous starfield file used for its twinkle keyframes.
// `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` disables all of them, matching that
// same file's pattern. Kept because the motion is what sells "glass
// panels drifting," not just static decoration — dropping it would lose
// the point of the preview.
// EXTRACTED (later pass): these keyframes/classes (`glass-float-a/b/c`
// and the `-reverse`/`-fast` variants) originally lived in this file's
// own inline <style> block. They've since been moved to
// `src/styles/float-animation.css` (imported globally via global.css) so
// other components can reuse the same drift animation without
// redefining it — this file's markup below is unchanged, it just now
// sources those classes globally instead of locally.
---

<div class:list={['pointer-events-none absolute -z-[5] top-24 sm:top-28 lg:top-32 inset-x-0 bottom-28 sm:bottom-40', className]}
  aria-hidden="true"
>
  <!-- s1 — top-left tall slab, blue tint -->
  <div class="glass-float-a absolute w-56 h-80 top-[-6%] left-[-4%] rotate-[-18deg] skew-y-[-4deg] overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-white/80 bg-gradient-to-br from-white/90 via-white/45 to-white/20 shadow-2xl">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-600/30 to-transparent"></div>
    <div class="absolute left-[12%] top-[10%] h-2 w-14 rotate-[-15deg] rounded-full bg-white/90 blur-sm"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- s2 — top-right block, no tint -->
  <div class="glass-float-b absolute w-64 h-56 top-[4%] right-[-6%] rotate-[22deg] skew-x-[-6deg] overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-white/80 bg-gradient-to-br from-white/90 via-white/45 to-white/20 shadow-2xl">
    <div class="absolute left-[12%] top-[10%] h-2 w-12 rotate-[-15deg] rounded-full bg-white/90 blur-sm"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- s3 — bottom-left small chip, amber tint -->
  <div class="glass-float-c absolute w-40 h-40 bottom-[-8%] left-[4%] rotate-[35deg] overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-white/80 bg-gradient-to-br from-white/90 via-white/45 to-white/20 shadow-2xl">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-amber-500/30 to-transparent"></div>
    <div class="absolute left-[12%] top-[10%] h-2 w-10 rotate-[-15deg] rounded-full bg-white/90 blur-sm"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- s4 — bottom-right large angled block, teal tint. Nudged up ~35px
       from its original bottom-[-10%] via a calc() offset (not a
       translate/transform utility — glass-float-a-reverse's keyframes
       already drive `transform` on this element, and a running CSS
       animation always wins that property over a static transform
       class, so the shift has to happen on `bottom` itself instead). -->
  <div class="glass-float-a-reverse absolute w-72 h-64 bottom-[calc(-10%+35px)] right-[2%] rotate-[-12deg] skew-y-[5deg] overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-white/80 bg-gradient-to-br from-white/90 via-white/45 to-white/20 shadow-2xl">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-teal-600/30 to-transparent"></div>
    <div class="absolute left-[12%] top-[10%] h-2 w-16 rotate-[-15deg] rounded-full bg-white/90 blur-sm"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- s5 — right-mid thin sliver, no tint -->
  <div class="glass-float-b-fast absolute w-28 h-56 top-[40%] right-[-3%] rotate-[8deg] skew-x-[10deg] overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-white/80 bg-gradient-to-br from-white/90 via-white/45 to-white/20 shadow-2xl">
    <div class="absolute left-[12%] top-[10%] h-2 w-10 rotate-[-15deg] rounded-full bg-white/90 blur-sm"></div>
  </div>
</div>
